window.AG_CHAPTERS["07"] = {"id":"07","title":"The Kiln Master&#39;s Dry Cough","titleZh":"窯場的乾咳","patient":{"name":"Wu Shen 吳嬸","sprite":"girl"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-garden.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Lung Yin Deficiency 肺陰虛","principle":"nourish Lung yin and moisten what has dried","tongue":"red body, little coating","pulseNote":{"en":"Fine under the finger and quicker than it should be — narrow, and hurrying.","zh":"按之細，數而不安，脈道不充而行速"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>Tàiyuān LU9</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"LU9","zh":"太淵","py":"Tàiyuān","x":140,"y":652,"img":"art/body-forearm-palmar.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"decoys":[{"x":160,"y":158},{"x":185,"y":571},{"x":150,"y":610},{"x":120,"y":760},{"x":200,"y":400}],"note":"<b>太淵 Tàiyuān LU9</b> — at the radial end of the wrist crease, in the depression where the radial artery pulses. Source point of the Lung and Influential point of the vessels.<br>腕橫紋橈側端，橈動脈搏動處陷中。肺之原穴，八會穴之脈會。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Ask about the <b>phlegm</b> first — how much, what colour, how easily it comes. Then ask when in the day she feels warm.","zh":"先問其痰：多寡、色質、易咯與否。再問一日之中何時覺熱。"},"look":{"en":"A red body with <b>little or no coating</b> is the signature. Coating is made from stomach qi and fluids — where it has thinned, fluids are short.","zh":"舌紅而少苔為其標誌。苔由胃氣津液所生，苔少則津虧。"},"pulse":{"en":"Two things at once: narrow because fluids are short, and quick because emptiness has bred heat.","zh":"二事同見：津虧則脈細，虛熱則脈數。"},"dx":{"en":"Which organ → deficiency or excess → and if deficient, deficient of <b>what</b>. Qi, blood and yin are not interchangeable.","zh":"何臟 → 虛實 → 若虛，虛在何物。氣、血、陰，不可混同。"},"rx":{"en":"You are refilling, not clearing. Reach for the Source point of the Lung, and for the water below that moistens it.","zh":"此為填補，非清瀉。取肺之原穴，並取下焦之水以潤之。"},"tech":{"en":"Reinforce gently. And ask yourself whether warmth helps or harms a patient who is already too dry.","zh":"補而宜輕。且當自問：其人已燥，加溫是助是害？"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen listens to her cough with his eyes closed. \"Again.\"","zh":"參師父閉著眼聽她咳。「再問。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"Wu Shen coughs twice, dryly, and nothing comes up.","zh":"吳嬸乾咳兩聲，咯不出東西。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy pours her water without being asked.","zh":"藥童沒等吩咐就給她倒了水。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Twenty years at the kiln,\" he says. \"Heat and dust, every day. Dryness does not arrive overnight.\"","zh":"「在窯上二十年，」他說，「日日火與塵。燥不是一夜來的。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"It is worse in the afternoon,\" she offers. \"And I wake with the sheets damp.\"","zh":"「午後重些，」她說，「醒來被褥是潮的。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Hold that. Damp sheets at night mean something quite specific.\"","zh":"「記住這句。夜間汗濕，所指甚明。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"cold_heat"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Moisten the Dry","cardZh":"潤燥","cardTxt":"Heat from emptiness is not put out by cooling — cooling an empty patient makes them emptier. Refill the fluids, and the heat has nothing left to rise from.","herbId":"baihe","herbEn":"Lily Bulb","herbZh":"百合","herbImg":"art/card-baihe.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet and slightly cold. It moistens the Lung and stops a dry cough, and quiets a mind made restless by heat — dryness and irritability answered together."},"endings":{"three":["A month later Wu Shen's cough is occasional and the night sweats have stopped. \"I had forgotten what it was like to sleep dry,\" she says.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You saw heat and did not reach for cold. That restraint is most of the skill.\"","一個月後，吳嬸咳嗽已稀，盜汗亦止。「我都忘了睡覺不出汗是什麼感覺。」她說。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你見了熱，卻沒有去清它。這一份克制，就是大半的功夫。」"],"two":["The cough eases; the night sweats persist.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You treated the Lung. You did not treat what feeds it from below.\"","咳嗽緩了，盜汗仍在。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你治了肺，卻未治其下所以養之者。」"],"one":["No change, and her throat is drier than when she came in.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Look at the coating again. It was telling you not to drain.\"","沒有起色，咽反更乾。<br><b>參師父：</b>「再看一次舌苔。它早告訴你不可用瀉。」"],"titles":["Wu Shen Sleeps Dry","Wu Shen Coughs Less","Wu Shen Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Chapter one was a cough. This is a cough too. They have almost nothing else in common.","cn":"第一章是咳嗽，這一章也是咳嗽。除此之外，幾乎毫無共通。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. I'm Wu, I tend the kiln on the west slope. This cough has been with me two years.","cn":"大夫。我姓吳，在西坡看窯。這咳嗽跟了我兩年。"},{"w":"patient","en":"It's dry. Almost nothing comes up, and what does is sticky. My throat feels scraped.","cn":"是乾咳。幾乎咯不出，咯出來也是黏的。咽喉像被刮過。"},{"w":"master","en":"Two years, dry, scanty sticky phlegm. Nothing about that is an invasion from outside.","cn":"兩年、乾咳、痰少而黏。此非外邪所襲。"},{"w":"master","en":"When a cough lasts this long, stop asking what came in. Start asking what has run out.","cn":"咳久若此，不必再問何邪入侵，當問何物已竭。"}],"qa":[{"q":"What is the phlegm like — how much, what colour?","cq":"痰如何？量多少？何色？","good":1,"a":"Hardly any. What there is comes up sticky and hard, and once there was a thread of blood.","ca":"幾乎沒有。有也是黏稠難咯，有一回還帶了血絲。","clue":{"en":"Scanty sticky phlegm, once blood-streaked","zh":"痰少黏稠，曾帶血絲"},"note":"Scanty sticky phlegm is dryness, not damp. Damp gives copious phlegm that comes up easily. A thread of blood means the dryness has begun to injure the collaterals. 痰少而黏為燥，非濕。濕則痰多易咯。痰中帶血，燥已傷絡。"},{"q":"Do you sweat at night?","cq":"夜間出汗嗎？","good":1,"a":"Yes. I wake and the sheets are damp, though I don't feel hot.","ca":"會。醒來被褥是潮的，人卻不覺得熱。","clue":{"en":"Night sweats","zh":"盜汗"},"note":"<b>Night sweats are yin deficiency.</b> Sweating by day on exertion is qi deficiency; sweating in sleep, unfelt, is yin failing to hold the fluids in. 盜汗屬陰虛。日間動則汗出為氣虛；寐中汗出而不自知，乃陰不斂液。"},{"q":"Is there a time of day when you feel warm?","cq":"一日之中，何時覺熱？","good":1,"a":"Late afternoon. A low warmth that comes up in my cheeks.","ca":"午後。一股低熱，泛在顴上。","clue":{"en":"Afternoon low fever, malar flush","zh":"午後低熱、顴紅"},"note":"Tidal warmth in the afternoon with flushed cheekbones is empty heat — heat that rises because yin has thinned, not because a pathogen is burning. 午後潮熱、顴紅為虛熱：陰虧而熱浮，非邪火燔灼。"},{"q":"Do you sweat during the day when you exert yourself, and do you catch colds easily?","cq":"白天勞動時出汗嗎？容易感冒嗎？","good":1,"a":"No more than anyone. And I rarely catch anything.","ca":"跟旁人差不多。也很少著涼。","clue":{"en":"No spontaneous sweating, not prone to colds","zh":"無自汗、不易感冒"},"note":"The exclusion that separates this from <b>Lung qi deficiency</b>, which brings a weak cough, spontaneous daytime sweating and frequent colds from unguarded wei qi. 此問分肺氣虛：肺氣虛者咳聲低弱、自汗、衛外不固而易感冒。"},{"q":"Do you have chills and fever, or a sore throat?","cq":"有惡寒發熱嗎？咽痛嗎？","good":0,"a":"No. Nothing like a cold.","ca":"沒有。不像著涼。","clue":"","note":"A reasonable exclusion, and negative. Chills with fever would place the illness on the exterior — impossible in a two-year cough anyway. 排除得當，惟為陰性。惡寒發熱屬表證，二年之咳亦不可能在表。"},{"q":"How is your appetite and are your stools loose?","cq":"胃口如何？大便溏嗎？","good":0,"a":"Appetite is fine. Stools are on the dry side, if anything.","ca":"胃口還好。大便反倒偏乾。","clue":"","note":"Sensible to check the Spleen, but negative here — and dry stools quietly support the dryness picture rather than contradicting it. 察脾為當，惟本案為陰性；便偏乾反佐燥證。"}],"look":[{"t":"Red body with little coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Red tongue, scant coat","zh":"舌紅少苔"},"note":"Correct. Red says heat; scant coating says fluids are short. Together they mean the heat comes <b>from</b> the shortage, which is the whole distinction of an empty-heat pattern. 是。紅主熱，少苔主津虧。二者合，則熱因虧而生——此正虛熱之所以為虛熱。"},{"t":"Red body with a thick yellow coat","c":"舌紅、苔黃厚","ok":0,"note":"That is full heat with a substantial pathogen — phlegm-heat in the Lung, with copious thick yellow sputum and fever. She has almost no phlegm at all. 此為實熱有形，痰熱壅肺，當見黃稠痰多而發熱。本案幾無痰。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat","c":"舌淡苔薄白","ok":0,"note":"Pale is emptiness without heat — Lung qi deficiency. But then you would expect spontaneous sweating and frequent colds, and no night sweats. 舌淡為虛而無熱，屬肺氣虛。然當見自汗易感冒，且無盜汗。"},{"t":"Pale swollen body with a white greasy coat","c":"舌淡胖、苔白膩","ok":0,"note":"Damp-phlegm. Copious phlegm, chest oppression, heavy limbs — the opposite of dryness in every respect. 此為痰濕：痰多、胸悶、身重，與燥證處處相反。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Thready and rapid 細數","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Thready rapid pulse","zh":"脈細數"},"note":"Correct, and it is two readings in one. Thready: not enough fluid to fill the vessel. Rapid: heat — but heat born of that shortage, so it is quick without being forceful. 是，一脈而兼二義。細者津不充脈，數者熱也——熱由虧生，故數而不甚有力。"},{"t":"Slippery and rapid 滑數","ok":0,"note":"Slippery means something substantial is moving in the vessel — phlegm. That belongs to phlegm-heat, not to dryness. 滑主有形之邪，屬痰。此為痰熱，非燥證。"},{"t":"Floating and tight 浮緊","ok":0,"note":"An exterior wind-cold pulse. Two years is not an exterior pattern. 此為外感風寒之脈。二年之病，不在表。"},{"t":"Weak 弱","ok":0,"note":"Plain emptiness with no heat — Lung qi deficiency. Her afternoon fever and night sweats say heat is present. 純虛無熱，屬肺氣虛。本案午後潮熱、盜汗，熱象確在。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — which organ?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：病在何臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Lung","c":"肺","ok":1,"note":"Cough, phlegm, a scraped throat, and twenty years of heat and kiln dust drawn in through the nose. The Lung governs qi and breathing and opens into the nose. 咳、痰、咽燥，二十年火塵自鼻而入。肺主氣司呼吸，開竅於鼻。"},{"t":"Kidney","c":"腎","ok":0,"note":"The Kidney is the deeper root of any long yin deficiency, and treating it is right — but the disorder presents in the Lung. Name where it is before naming where it came from. 久病陰虛，其根固在腎，治之亦當；然病現於肺。先定其所在，再論其所自。"},{"t":"Stomach","c":"胃","ok":0,"note":"Stomach yin deficiency gives hunger without desire to eat, epigastric burning and a mirror tongue. Her appetite is fine. 胃陰虛者饑不欲食、胃中嘈雜灼痛、鏡面舌。本案納可。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — deficiency or excess?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：虛實何屬？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Deficiency","c":"虛","ok":1,"note":"Two years, gradual, scanty phlegm, a thinning tongue coat, a pulse that is quick but not forceful. Excess heat is loud and has substance; this is quiet and thin. 病程二年、緩起、痰少、苔漸剝、脈數而不有力。實熱聲勢有形，此則靜而薄。"},{"t":"Excess — phlegm-heat obstructing the Lung","c":"實 — 痰熱壅肺","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm-heat brings copious thick yellow sputum, fever, chest pain, a greasy yellow coat and a slippery rapid pulse. She has scanty sticky phlegm and a peeling tongue. 痰熱壅肺當見黃稠痰多、發熱、胸痛、苔黃膩、脈滑數。本案痰少而黏、舌苔剝落。"},{"t":"Mixed — an exterior pathogen on a deficient base","c":"虛實夾雜 — 表邪兼虛","ok":0,"note":"There is no exterior pathogen: no chills, no fever with aversion to wind, no sudden onset. 本案無表邪：不惡寒、不發熱惡風、非驟起。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — deficient of what? Qi, blood, or yin?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：虛在何物？氣？血？陰？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Yin — because heat came with the emptiness","c":"陰虛 — 虛而生熱","ok":1,"note":"<b>This is the step that decides everything.</b> Qi deficiency: spontaneous daytime sweating, frequent colds, pale tongue, weak pulse — <i>no heat</i>. Yin deficiency: night sweats, afternoon tidal warmth, malar flush, red tongue with scant coat, thready rapid pulse — <i>heat born of emptiness</i>. She has the second set entirely. 此步定全局。氣虛者：自汗、易感冒、舌淡、脈弱，無熱。陰虛者：盜汗、午後潮熱、顴紅、舌紅少苔、脈細數，虛而生熱。本案全屬後者。"},{"t":"Qi — the Lung's protective function has weakened","c":"氣虛 — 衛外不固","ok":0,"note":"Then she would sweat by day, tire on exertion and catch every cold that passed through the village. She told you she rarely catches anything. 若然，當日間自汗、動則氣短、易感風寒。其言少有著涼。"},{"t":"Blood — the Lung is not being nourished","c":"血虛 — 肺失所養","ok":0,"note":"Blood deficiency shows in colour: pale face, pale lips and nails, pale tongue. Hers is red. And blood deficiency brings no fever. 血虛見於色：面唇甲淡、舌淡。本案舌紅，且血虛不發熱。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"LU9","t":"Tàiyuān LU9 太淵","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Lung — the point for Lung deficiency of any kind, and the one to reach for when the organ itself is depleted rather than obstructed. It is also the Influential point of the vessels. 肺之原穴。凡肺虛皆可取之，臟自虧者尤宜，非為邪阻而設。又為八會之脈會。"},{"id":"KI3","t":"Tàixī KI3 太谿","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Kidney. In a long yin deficiency the Lung is where it shows and the Kidney is where it is refilled — metal and water nourish each other. 腎之原穴。久病陰虧，見於肺而補於腎，金水相生。"},{"id":"SP6","t":"Sānyīnjiāo SP6 三陰交","ok":1,"note":"Where the three leg yin channels cross — one needle nourishing yin on three fronts at once, which is why it belongs in almost any yin-deficient prescription. 足三陰交會之處，一針而三陰俱滋。凡陰虛之方多用之。"},{"id":"LU5","t":"Chǐzé LU5 尺澤","ok":0,"note":"The Sea point of the Lung, and it <b>drains</b>. Correct for a hot full Lung with thick yellow phlegm; wrong for a Lung that has run dry. Draining an empty patient is how you make her worse. 肺經合穴，主瀉。宜於肺實熱、痰黃稠者；肺燥津虧則不宜。虛而瀉之，是益其病。"},{"id":"ST40","t":"Fēnglóng ST40 豐隆","ok":0,"note":"Transforms phlegm. She has almost no phlegm — there is nothing to transform, and the point is drying by nature, which is the last thing a dry patient needs. 化痰之穴。本案幾無痰可化，且其性主燥，於燥者尤忌。"},{"id":"LI4","t":"Hégǔ LI4 合谷","ok":0,"note":"Releases the exterior and moves qi strongly. No exterior pattern, and strong movement disperses fluids that are already short. 解表行氣力強。本案無表證，且強行則散其已虧之津。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, gentle and shallow, no moxa","c":"補法，宜輕宜淺，不施灸","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and the second half is the point. Yin deficiency is reinforced — but <b>moxa warms and dries</b>, and this patient is already too dry and running warm in the afternoons. Emptiness does not automatically mean warm it. 是，而要義在後半。陰虛當補，然灸性溫燥，其人已燥且午後有熱。虛者未必宜溫。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method with generous moxa to strengthen her","c":"補法，重灸以壯其虛","ok":0,"note":"The instinct to tonify is right; the moxa is not. Warming an empty-heat pattern adds fuel to a fire that is burning because there is too little water. 欲補之念不誤，而灸則非。虛熱者加溫，是以火濟火，其火本因水少。"},{"t":"Reducing method to clear the heat","c":"瀉法以清其熱","ok":0,"note":"The heat is real but it is <b>empty</b> heat. Draining it removes what little substance she has left and the heat returns worse. 熱雖實有，然為虛熱。瀉之則奪其僅存之陰，熱反更甚。"},{"t":"Prick to bleed at LU11 for the throat","c":"少商點刺放血以利咽","ok":0,"note":"That is the method for an acute hot sore throat — a full pattern. Bleeding a patient whose fluids are already short is the wrong direction entirely. 此為急性熱毒咽痛之法，屬實證。津虧者刺血，適得其反。"}]};
